prompt:
Our hitch catcher (src/ReplicatedStorage/Shared/Dev/HitchSnapshot.luau) saves the MicroProfiler's frames to slot 2 when a playtest hitches. Add src/ReplicatedStorage/Shared/Dev/SpikeReport.luau with a function run(slot: number) that we'll call from the Studio command bar in Edit mode after the playtest, like require(game.ReplicatedStorage.Shared.Dev.SpikeReport).run(2). Dev modules get LibMP through LibMPLoader in the same folder.

For the snapshot in that slot, run should return a table with:

- the median and 90th percentile frame time;
- every frame that took more than twice the median, each with the five scopes that spent the most time of their own in that frame (not counting time spent in scopes nested inside them), across the CPU threads;
- the same top five, averaged over the frames that weren't slow, so we can compare a hitch with a normal frame.

Name each slow frame so we can find it both from LibMP and in the MicroProfiler UI.
